  "question": {
    "text": "When enthanol is heated with conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, a gas is produced. The compound formed, when this gas is treated with cold dilute aqueous solution of Baeyer&#39;s reagent, is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Formaldehyde",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Formic acid",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Glycol",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Ethanoic acid",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Ethanol undergoes dehydration by heating it with concentrated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>443</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mn>443</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>Alkenes on reaction with cold, dilute, aqueous solution of potassium permanganate (Baeyer&rsquo;s reagent) produce vicinal glycols. Decolorisatlon of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution is used as a test for unsaturation.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0061_b622c1de37db.png\" style=\"width: 451px; height: 149px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
